(Progressive delivery) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Every Orion release starts with a 5 percent canary for 15 minutes. If the) Tj
T*
(guardrails stay healthy, traffic increases to 25 percent for another 15) Tj
T*
(minutes, then to 100 percent. The release controller records each promotion.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Automatic rollback begins when the error rate rises by more than 1 percentage) Tj
T*
(point above baseline or when p95 latency remains above 400 milliseconds for) Tj
T*
(five consecutive minutes. A feature flag is not a substitute for rollback;) Tj
T*
(the on-call engineer must confirm that the previous build is healthy.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Database migrations must be backward compatible for one complete release.) Tj
T*
(Destructive schema changes require a separate reviewed cleanup release.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
